==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sick Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Prisoner Cat''' when obtained from the [[Adult Cat Awakes!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Before True Form, Adult Cat and Sick Cat are basically useless. Even in early-game, other attackers can replace them, and in anything later than early-game, they will only serve to increase your [[User Rank]] or [[Cat Combo|Combos]].

==='''True Form'''===
Prisoner Cat becomes a powerful ranged attacker, easily able to help deal with threats like [[Master A.]] and [[THE SLOTH]]. Keep in mind that Prisoner Cat is defenseless if an enemy gets in his decently sized blindspot. He also only has 25 inner range, so enemies who are not properly crowd-controlled can enter provided you have not protected Prisoner well. Try and use good defense coupled with cats that can knock back enemies to keep this from happening. It is important to note that when hypermaxed and stacked, Prisoner Cat is quite useful in 4-crowns [[Stories of Legend]], as this Cats ability to attack from a safe range is incredibly rare and uncommon, especially among almost all Rare and Special Cats.

Additionally, Prisoner Cat's large blindspot allows him to be stacked on stages such as [[Deathhawk (Deadly)|Deathhawk]]. This makes him one of the best non-Gacha ways to counter [[Professor A.|Professor A]], with a priceless role in stages like [[Pecking Order]], [[Tiny Meows (Deadly)|Tiny Meows]] or [[Saucy Scandals]]. However, this usefulness is determined by the amount you are able to stack him, as his lack of survivability and two knockbacks can be his downfall if not kept safe.

By the time you reach [[Uncanny Legends]], his damage quickly proves to be unviable. Combined with his atrocious recharge time and target range, this makes him unreliable at the best of times.

